; NS_SERIAL_MISMATCH — a zone transfer that stopped.
;
; Served by both dns-auth and dns-divergent, with different SOA serials. Every
; answer either gives is valid; one of them is simply older, and which one a
; customer sees depends on which server their resolver happened to pick. This
; is the fault that produces "it works for me" with nobody lying.
;
; Keep in step with zones/divergent/drift.test.zone, which is the stale side.
$ORIGIN drift.test.
$TTL 300

@       IN SOA  ns1.test. hostmaster.propgate.invalid. (
                7 7200 3600 1209600 300 )
@       IN NS   ns1.test.
@       IN NS   ns-divergent.test.

www     IN A    198.51.100.70
